==English==
{{was wotd|2019|March|20}}

===Etymology===
A reference to {{m|en|teething||the [[eruption]], through the [[gum#Noun|gums]], of the [[milk teeth]]}} and the accompanying [[discomfort]], which occur during early life.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈtiːðɪŋ ˈtɹʌb(ə)lz/|lang=en}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|/ˈtiðɪŋ ˈtɹʌb(ə)lz/|/ˈtɹə-/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-au-teething troubles.ogg|Audio (AU)|lang=en}}
* {{hyphenation|teeth|ing trou|bles|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-plural noun|head=[[teething]] [[trouble]]s}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} Small [[problem]]s such as are to be [[expect#Verb|expected]] with any [[new]] and [[untried]] [[product]], [[system]], or [[venture#Noun|venture]].
#: {{synonyms|en|teething issues|teething problems}}
#* {{quote-book|author=R. Emerick|chapter=Mr. R. Emerick, Mr. S. Clegg, Mr. T. Warburton, on Behalf of the Amalgamated Society of Lithographic Printers|title=Royal Commission on the Press: Minutes of Oral Evidence{{nb...|[...] Present to Parliament by the Prime Minister by Command of Her Majesty}}|series=Cmnd. 1812|location=London|publisher=[[w:Office of Public Sector Information|Her Majesty’s Stationery Office]]|date=16 October 1961|year_published=September 1962|volume=II (Witnesses: Trades Unions and Associations,{{nb...|Wholesale and Retail Distribution Companies and Associations, Paper Manufacturers and Import Agents, Advertising Agents and Institute of Practitioners in Advertising}})|section=paragraph 9041|page=25|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=ChY0AQAAMAAJ&pg=PA25|oclc=1015674316|passage=But we think that, for something which is so new, it is far better and easier for them to recoup if it is only a 16,000 run. If it is up in the millions it is a bigger problem, and it is far better to get your '''teething troubles''' out of the way on a smaller one.|lang=en}}

